cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Janus or its data, please cite it as below, with the version you used."
title: "Janus: open tools to find prescribing cascades in medication lists"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Üstüner"
    given-names: "Mikail"
version: "0.2.2"
date-released: "2026-11-13"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/mikailustuner/janus"
url: "https://janusmeds.org"
abstract: >-
  Janus checks a medication list for 65 published prescribing cascades (the PIPC list) and explains each
  pattern for a conversation with a doctor. It ships open data and tools for researchers: a FAERS onset table,
  data-quality reports and an experimental drug model starter kit. Research prototype, not a medical device.
  Expert review has not yet been done.
keywords:
  - prescribing cascade
  - polypharmacy
  - pharmacovigilance
  - FAERS
  - deprescribing
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Potentially inappropriate prescribing cascades (PIPC) list"
    authors:
      - family-names: "Rochon"
        given-names: "Paula A."
    journal: "European Geriatric Medicine"
    year: 2025
    volume: 16
    issue: 5
    start: 1573
    end: 1584
    doi: "10.1007/s41999-025-01215-x"
